                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Under direction of the Legal Support Staff Services Manager, Assistant Chief Counsel, General Counsel, and the general direction of Staff Counsel, the Legal Analyst performs the following:</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"></span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">&nbsp;<br /></span></span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 11pt;">Coordinates all Petitions for Reinstatement and makes preliminary determinations of eligibility for reinstatement for attorney approval. &nbsp;Prepares Petition agenda packets for the Commission. Schedules Petitions for Reinstatement, ALJ Proposed Decisions, transcript reviews, and Decision and Orders for Commission review. Monitors and analyzes ALJ Proposed Decisions from the Office of Administrative Hearings. Assists with preparing the Commission’s Closed Session agenda. </span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 11pt;">Assists in all aspects related to the Committee of Credentials (Committee). This includes scheduling hearings before the Committee, creating the Committee’s agenda, recording Committee meeting minutes as recording secretary, and working with other Legal Office staff and Commission staff in preparation for meetings. Organizes and prepares all correspondence related to procedures and outcomes for the Committee. Responds to procedural questions both orally and in writing from respondents and their counsel appearing before the Committee. Ensures that all Committee members’ Travel Expense Claims (TEC) are prepared and input into the CALATERS system for processing and payment.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 11pt;">Assists with performing analyses, collects records, and assists in drafting appropriate agency responses, in conjunction with the Office of the Attorney General and Commission staff counsel, in response to litigation, including, motions to compel and subpoenas, and requests for records under the Public Records Act and the Information Practices Act. Responds to sensitive, high level inquiries concerning Commission actions, and provides analytical support to Commission staff regarding data and records requests.<br /><br /> </span></p><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0pt; color: #333333; font-family: &quot;Source Sans Pro&quot;, sans-serif; text-decoration-color: initial; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;">This advertisement will run until filled with the following cutoff dates for review of applications:</strong></span></span></p><ul style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 11px; color: #333333; font-family: &quot;Source Sans Pro&quot;, sans-serif; text-decoration-color: initial;"><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">March 13, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">March 24, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">April 3, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">April 14, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">April 24, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">May 5, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">May 15, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li><li style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;"><strong style="box-sizing: border-box;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial;">May 26, 2025</span></strong></span></span></li></ul><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"> </span></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25932019&name=DutyStatement-LegalAnalystfinalversion041824.pdf' target='_blank'>D